    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62654,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 123,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovarian stroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:40:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62655,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 123,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibromatosis and massive oedema present in premenopausal patients, with menstrual abnormalities, abdominal pain, or androgenic manifestations {6490313}. Most cases are unilateral {6490313; 8729041}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:40:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62656,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 123,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are rare lesions.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:40:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62657,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 123,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See below.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:40:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62658,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 123,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovarian fibromatosis is a stromal proliferation unrelated to the fibromatosis of soft tissue type {9421079}. It may rarely be associated with overgrowth disorders {23333153}. Massive oedema is associated with ovarian torsion, and obstruction of venous/lymphatic drainage is thought to play an etiological role {6490313; 17717430}. It is also associated with fibromatosis and benign/malignant neoplastic conditions, possibly through similar mechanisms {6490313; 15099983; 24901402}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:40:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62659,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 123,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The ovary is enlarged (average: 8&nbsp;cm), with a smooth nodular surface and a cut surface that is firm (fibromatosis) or watery (massive oedema) {6490313; 8729041}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:40:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62660,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 123,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibromatosis is a proliferation of ovarian stromal fibroblastic cells with variable collagen deposition. Massive oedema shows markedly oedematous stroma that spares the outermost cortex. Luteinized stromal cells can be seen. Both processes preserve pre-existing ovarian structures {6490313; 8729041; 17717430}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:40:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62661,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 123,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:40:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62662,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 123,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:40:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62663,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 123,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> fibromatosis: fibroblastic stromal proliferation with collagen deposition; massive oedema: stromal accumulation of oedema fluid.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:40:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
